ue "CRD"} "Cycling Road"] "\n" [:option {:value "CTR"} "Cycling Track"] "\n" [:option {:value "DIV"} "Diving"] "\n" [:option {:value "FEN"} "Fencing"] "\n" [:option {:value "FBL"} "Football"] "\n" [:option {:value "SHO"} "Shooting"] "\n" [:option {:value "SWM"} "Swimming"] "\n" [:option {:value "TEN"} "Tennis"] "\n" [:option {:value "TOW"} "Tug-Of-War"] "\n" [:option {:value "WLF"} "Weightlifting"] "\n" [:option {:value "WRE"} "Wrestling"]]] [:script {} "$('#sports_in_same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/editions/4/sports/'+$('#sports_in_same_games_select').val()})"] [:form {:id "other_games_form", :class "form-inline", :style "display: inline", :method "get"} [:select {:name "year", :id "sport_in_other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "Rowing in other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "1"} "1896 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "2"} "1900 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "3"} "1904 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "5"} "1908 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "6"} "1912 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "7"} "1920 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "8"} "1924 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "9"} "1928 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "10"} "1932 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "11"} "1936 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "12"} "1948 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "13"} "1952 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "14"} "1956 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "15"} "1960 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "16"} "1964 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "17"} "1968 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "18"} "1972 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "19"} "1976 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "20"} "1980 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "21"} "1984 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "22"} "1988 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "23"} "1992 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "24"} "1996 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "25"} "2000 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "26"} "2004 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "53"} "2008 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "65"} "2010 Summer Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "54"} "2012 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "67"} "2014 Summer Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "59"} "2016 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "69"} "2018 Summer Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "61"} "2020 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "63"} "2024 Summer Olympics"]]] [:script {} "$('#sport_in_other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/editions/' + $('#sport_in_other_games_select').val() + '/sports/ROW'})"] "\n" [:h1 {} "Rowing at the 1906  Intercalated Games"] "\n" [:table {:class "biodata"} "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Dates"] "\n" [:td {} "24 – 27 April 1906"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Medal Events"] "\n" [:td {} "6"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Venues"] "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/214"} "Ormos Falirou, Peiraias"]] "\n"] "\n"]] "\n" [:div {:class "description"} "\n" [:p {} "The rowing events of 1906 were conducted on the open water in the " [:a {:href "/venues/214"} "Faliron Bay"] ", as were the " [:a {:href "/editions/4/sports/SWM"} "swimming"] " and " [:a {:href "/editions/4/sports/DIV"} "diving"] " events.  As with the swimming, several of the rowing events had to be postponed on 25-26 April [12-13 April] when heavy winds raised the Falirou sea into huge waves, which made the holding of rowing events dangerous.  There were six events held in the 1906 rowing competition: " [:a {:href "/results/157533"} "single sculls"] ", " [:a {:href "/results/157534"} "coxed pairs over 1-kilometer"] ", " [:a {:href "/results/157535"} "coxed pairs over 1-mile"] ", " [:a {:href "/results/157536"} "coxed fours over 2000-meters"] ", " [:a {:href "/results/157537"} "6-man naval rowing boats over 2000-meters"] ", and " [:a {:href "/results/157538"} "16-man naval rowing boats over 3000-meters"] "."] "\n\n" [:p {} "A few notes are in order.  The single sculls event was held over 1000-meters. It is listed in the official programme as “Course de Canoë”.  However, this only appears to be a Greek difficulty translating French in the official results and the programme.  There were only two rowers in this event, both from France, and the winner was " [:a {:href "/athletes/14121"} "Gaston Delaplane"] ".  Pictures in the French sporting magazine " [:em {} "La Vie Au Grand Air"] " show pictures of Delaplane in a standard scull.  Interestingly, in the official entry lists, there are no entries listed for the singles event."] "\n\n" [:p {} "It is highly unusual that there were two coxed pairs events, one over 1-kilometer and one over 1-mile, and we have no explanation for why this was so.  The Belgian team in these events, the Orban brothers, " [:a {:href "/athletes/79843"} "Max"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/35728"} "Rémy"] ", representing the Société Nautique de Gand, came to Athens on their own with no coxswain.  Apparently, they did not know that a coxswain would be required.  They recruited a young Greek man, named " [:a {:href "/athletes/80152"} "Theofilakos Psiliakos"] ", who served as the cox for them in both events.  In the 1-mile event, this combined Belgian/Greek team finished second, earning them a silver medal."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The naval rowing boats events are always listed as for 6-men and 16-men.  However, the boats were headed by coxswains as well, so, in actuality, there were 7 and 17 men in the boats in the two events.  The terminology in the English-language press was also slightly different than usually seen in Olympic reference books.  They termed the coxed pairs and coxed fours the “2-oar gigs” and “4-oar gigs.”  The larger boats were termed the “6-man galleys” and the “16-man galleys.”"] "\n\n" [:p {} "The top rowers in this era were considered to be the British, and possibly the Canadians.  Britain’s top sculler was " [:a {:href "/athletes/37350"} "Frederick Kelly"] ", who had won the Diamond Challenge Sculls at Henley in 1902-03 and 1905.  In 1904, Canada’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/36263"} "Lou Scholes"] " had defeated Kelly for that title, and he had won several Canadian and American championships.  The Americans were not considered quite as good, but still had some good rowers, notably the defending " [:a {:href "/results/157528"} "Olympic single sculls"] " champion, " [:a {:href "/athletes/40678"} "Frank Greer"] ", who was American champion in 1903-05 and 1908.  None of these three countries were represented at Athens in 1906 Olympic rowing."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:th {} "NOCs"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/157533"} "Single Sculls, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Intercalated"] "\n" [:td {} "27 April 1906"] "\n" [:td {} "2"] "\n" [:td {} "1"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/157534"} "Coxed Pairs (1 kilometre), Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Intercalated"] "\n" [:td {} "27 April 1906"] "\n" [:td {} "24"] "\n" [:td {} "5"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/157535"} "Coxed Pairs (1 mile), Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Intercalated"] "\n" [:td {} "27 April 1906"] "\n" [:td {} "21"] "\n" [:td {} "5"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/157536"} "Coxed Fours, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Intercalated"] "\n" [:td {} "24 April 1906"] "\n" [:td {} "40"] "\n" [:td {} "4"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/157537"} "7-Man Naval Rowing Boats, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Intercalated"] "\n" [:td {} "24 April 1906"] "\n" [:td {} "28"] "\n" [:td {} "2"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/157538"} "17-Man Naval Rowing Boats, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Intercalated"] "\n" [:td {} "24 April 1906"] "\n" [:td {} "85"] "\n" [:td {} "2"] "